WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.598
Text structure and purpose.

00:00:02.598 --> 00:00:04.578
Don't just ask what the author says.

00:00:04.578 --> 00:00:06.309
Ask what the author is doing.

00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:09.544
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:13.544
The question asks for the main purpose, or the overall structure.

00:00:13.544 --> 00:00:16.639
Or it asks about one underlined sentence.

00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:20.841
It's testing the job each part of the text is doing.

00:00:21.902 --> 00:00:23.177
Here's the method.

00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:28.772
Label each sentence with a verb: introduces, describes, challenges, concludes.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:32.347
For purpose, combine the labels into one main action.

00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:34.997
For structure, keep the actions in order.

00:00:34.997 --> 00:00:37.372
Then check every word of the answer.

00:00:37.372 --> 00:00:39.227
One wrong verb kills it.

00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:41.927
Check the verbs carefully.

00:00:41.927 --> 00:00:44.102
Describing is not arguing.

00:00:44.102 --> 00:00:46.427
Questioning is not disproving.

00:00:46.427 --> 00:00:49.852
Function means what a sentence does, not what it says.

00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:53.086
And in two-part answers, both halves must be right.

00:00:54.148 --> 00:00:55.368
Let's try one.

00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:57.018
Label each sentence.

00:00:57.018 --> 00:00:58.418
Many people believe.

00:00:58.418 --> 00:01:00.118
That's a common belief.

00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:02.208
Experiments tell a different story.

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:03.958
That's evidence against it.

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:05.608
Such results suggest.

00:01:05.608 --> 00:01:06.958
That's a conclusion.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:09.373
Belief, evidence, conclusion.

00:01:09.373 --> 00:01:11.498
A calls the experiment flawed.

00:01:11.498 --> 00:01:13.448
C brings in other animals.

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.348
D argues about cruelty.

00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:17.541
Only B has all three, in order.

00:01:18.585 --> 00:01:20.510
Watch out for the wrong verb.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:25.795
An answer that says argues, or criticizes, when the author only describes.

00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:28.331
One wrong word makes the whole choice wrong.

00:01:29.377 --> 00:01:31.262
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:31.262 --> 00:01:32.317
How to spot it.

00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.717
The four steps.

00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:35.032
The verb checks.

00:01:35.032 --> 00:01:36.057
And the trap.

00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:38.817
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
